Name: Enkidu (Enkidu is one of the oldest literary characters ever coming from Epic of Gilgamesh. Like how Limbus Company has each Sinner’s name is pulled from a famous work Dante → The Divine Comedy, Faust → Faust (Goethe), Don Quixote → Don Quixote (Cervantes), Ryōshū → Hell Screen. That’s why this character is called Enkidu).
Alias: The Earth’s Abnormality, The Green Chain, The Clay of Creation, Friend of The King.
Affiliation: Independent, can cooperate with others, can accept requests for free within his reasons and naturally caring for nature, managed to become Colored Fixer in a few weeks due to his abilities and became Green Chain, and was unnoticed by that he was Abnormality with clear human mind because he appeared human without any detections of being an abnormality.
Threat Level: ALEPH+ (beyond standard classification).
Status: Self-Actualized Abnormality” A Abnormality whose sense of self has achieved human intelligence to to absorb knowledge and logic, and no longer mindless mud of clay.
Gender: Unknown.
Height/Weight: 5’10”/??? lbs.
Alignment: Neutral Good.
Status: Alive.
E.G.O: Aeon of Babylon, and Aluma Alish.
Abnormality Classification (If asked): Above most Color Fixers and ALEPH abnormalities with just Aeon of Babylon, and capable of rivalling Gilgamesh with Apsû and being acknowledged as his only equal.
Scaling: Against the City. 95% of characters → near-effortless win. Color Fixers → heavily favored win, not guaranteed. Arbiter → dangerous matchup while he has the range, weapon, versatility and tactical advantage without Apsû. It is stated that Enkidu’s Aluma Alish is the counterbalance to Gilgamesh‘s Apsû.
Origin: Enkidu is Abnormality born outside the City and came the Outskirts and was a formless clump of mud, so they seek out a "complete human" to copy its form to be able to interact with humans. Later unknown woman who noticed Enkidu and thought of helping their lack of rational thought. The asexual lump of clay fell for the beauty of the woman, which transcended the bound between man and woman, and they spent six days and seven nights together. The mud puppet, ignorant of mankind, slowly allowed their form to approximate that of a human, which seemed to become that of the beautiful harlot sharing their food and bed with them, as if attempting to assume her beauty. Enkidu made her paradoxical beauty their own, losing much of their strength, though still retaining levels of both far above that of humanity, in exchange for wisdom and reason. They had never looked in a mirror, so the humanoid form became a good instructor for Enkidu to learn about themself. They acquired knowledge and rational thought, all the truths of the earth. Filled with the soul needed to notice its sense of self, Enkidu spoke their name for the first time and the world became something extremely simple in that instant. Upon encountering and understanding that Gilgamesh's arrogance stemmed from his solitude, Enkidu sought to reprimand him, but did not state the real reason to avoid hurting his pride. They met Gilgamesh the Outskirts, and both clashed in a fierce battle that lasted for several days. Gilgamesh was angered by a "clod of mud" being equal to him, humiliated that he had to use his treasures. He soon came to enjoy the battle, however, and brought his weapons out without regret. Gilgamesh decided to draw Apsû to perform Aluma Alish and Enkidu counter it with his own Aluma Alish which both attacks cancelled each other out. After fierce fighting that left them both spent, each warrior collapsed to the ground without consideration for the location. Gilgamesh did so laughing, noting that there could be no winner without two corpses, and Enkidu fell in imitation of him, like a mirror.

Appearance: Enkidu's appearance is something modeled after the unknown woman out of respect. Lancer is able to take a myriad of forms, but their usual form is that of an eighteen-year-old androgynous person with long, beautiful hair that shimmers with a light-green color. He doesn’t appear possess accessories to stand out, so they seem rather unremarkable compared to those normally called Colored Fixers. Enkidu doesn’t carry any item, and their clothing does not look valuable in any way. It is hard to tell if Enkidu is a man or woman at first glance. Their attire consists of a loose, flowing, tunic robe-like garment of pale ivory-white fabric, subtly tinted with cool mint and light blue-green hues. The garment features an open, softly folded neckline that exposes a small portion of the collarbones and upper chest, while its exceedingly wide, billowing sleeves create a voluminous silhouette reminiscent of traditional ceremonial clothing. The fabric falls asymmetrically around their body, forming broad, overlapping folds and angular draperies that extend to approximately knee level. Beneath the outer garment, they wear loose, muted teal trousers that narrow around the ankles, where pale fabric wraps or cuffs are visible. Their feet remain completely bare, revealing slender ankles and delicately defined toes, contributing to their natural, unadorned appearance. A particularly distinctive accessory is a long, slender, dark cord that hangs from around their neck and descends across the front of their clothing, terminating in a small, pointed, golden ornament resembling a narrow spearhead or arrowhead. The cord curves freely across their body, introducing a subtle contrast against the pale fabric. Their visible hand is slender and delicate, with long, graceful fingers held loosely at their side. Their face retains vaguely childlike features that are able to be interpreted as that of either gender. Their lustrous skin and soft features are reminiscent of a woman, but their loose tunic further obscures their sex by hiding their physique, making it impossible to see their chest and hips, and making it difficult to discern if they are even actually human. They have firm and taut limbs with rough hands and feet like those of men, and their body seems like a coiled spring ready to rocket forth. With an androgynous and neutral voice, Enkidu's face can be called beautiful and elegant despite their gender, but at the same time gives off a strange and uncomfortable atmosphere. While their face looks human, it also appears inhuman due to the fact that it looks "too perfect." While the feeling cannot be put into words and it is not immediately apparent to the eye, Enkidu's form evokes a similar feeling in the observer as a mannequin or puppets constructed by Wings or certain Association. Their nature becomes less apparent the more one looks upon them, but their beauty as a being of perfect harmony is undeniable. 

Personality: Enkidu originally didn't have a personality until they bonded with other humans and Gilgamesh himself. Enkidu seems to greatly appreciate nature, and often finds it as a relief that some parts of the world is still beautiful as ever even after being covered by cities. They are happy to sit while others nearby are resting and simply allow themself to enjoy the magnificent natural landscape and the "song of the river." Even when dealing with the person who try to attack him, Enkidu speaks serenely in a polite manner without any provocation. They can follow other's wishes exactly without issue, as long the wish isn’t mindless slaughter to test him. Much like Gilgamesh, Lancer regards their friendship highly. They held that they were a weapon in life, and that their fate was to be supplanted by the next. Any worth or mystery was to be limited only to Enkidu's age, but Gilgamesh changed those thoughts. Gilgamesh accepted a penalty of a fate of solitude thereafter, but granted Enkidu with a soul with his words. Enkidu believes that they sinned in knowing Gilgamesh, whose greatest sincerity was to remain aloof without acknowledging the strong or the weak, but in the end, Enkidu ended up leaving a lasting mar upon that integrity. Enkidu is extremely surprised upon learning Gilgamesh, and initially cannot even believe in such a turn of fate. After calmly opening their eyes, slowly standing up, and having a brief moment of silence, a feeling of confusion, frustration, and finally overwhelming joy rampages through their chest. Enkidu believes it is destiny that they will battle once again, and is confident that the tapestry woven between them and their King would not tear just because a fight or two. Even after a thousand melees together, their bond would remain just as strong as ever. Introverted, active and self-assured. Usually they just loiter like a beautiful flower; but, once they get on the move, they becomes a frightening active monster that doesn’t wait, has no mercy and shows no self-restraint. Since they are a life form born from the Earth, Enkidu also finds humans “appealing”. But, because humans think of themselves as beings apart from nature due to their intelligence, they rank low as protection targets. Enkidu feels that animals and plants are existences closer to themself and will mostly take action in order to protect them, rather than humans. That being said, since they had great curiosity (intellectual craving) to begin with, Enkidu regards conversations with humans as an enjoyment. If said character has an appealing personality (a totalitarian brimming with a philanthropic mentality, but still someone who thinks of themselves foremost), Enkidu will demonstrate respect and admiration from the bottom of their heart, feeling joy in supporting them as a friend.

E.G.O
Aeon of Babylon: is the primary E.G.O of Enkidu and Abnormality who’s nature has strong connection to the planet it stand on. It is their primary form of attack that they always use in battle. It is an equivalent to Gilgamesh's Coronation of Babylon which enables Enkidu to connect to the ground with chains and reproduce creations from the world’s memory. With it, Enkidu is able to create weapons, such as swords, spears, hammers and chains from the ground using clay. Each of these weapons represents the pinnacle of human craftsmanship. During their fight, Gilgamesh got to “fire” hundreds, maybe thousands, of E.G.O, with Enkidu equally matching him blow for blow. Enkidu can even reproduce famed and treasured E.G.O. Enkidu can activate this E.G.O over great distances, they were able to create spears of earth to appear in front of Gilgamesh to deflect attacks, despite still being in the forest a few kilometers away. Upon using it, Enkidu is able to utilize its true nature and reproduce the greatest weapons in the world, capable of erasing poorly built material with a touch. They can also create defensive golden walls capable of withstanding the very same weapons Enkidu fired at their foes. Aeon of Babylon has the special property of constantly “updating” with Enkidu. The ability to draw from the planet’s memory and produce various objects. The very act of copying human history is its true nature. Therefore, the longer time passes, the denser, higher, and deeper is the data they gain. Enkidu can expand the range of civilization they can replicate by connecting themself to many different eras. In the current present, Enkidu would be summoning numerous that can only be considered impossible fantasies nowadays. But due to Enkidu's very foundation being a powerful Distortion, all modern weapons they reproduce are empowered and made with an appearance that would fit. If Enkidu created a gatling gun, each individual bullet would be boosted with energy to destroy enemy Fixers. If they used the model of a fighter jet, it would be empowered enough to compete in a flying race against a Gilgamesh’s Varka. During their battle, Enkidu created eight 120mm anti-aircraft artillery cannons. The shells fired from them could take tricky trajectories that defied the laws of physics and packed enough power to exterminate an Abnormality in one hit. Additionally the rate of fire would accelerate throughout the battle, going up to 1 shot per second compared to the 12 rounds per minute that a usual anti-air craft cannon could manage. The reason why this E.G.O is comparable to Coronation of Babylon is due to this attribute. The number of weapons Enkidu shapes from dirt is the number created by world. That means they use the land as a means for mass production. Gilgamesh collected the pinnacle of human potential in his Coronation of Babylon. One of the articles stored there is Varka. Replicating that would, needless to say, require being summoned either in a far distant future, the era when humanity reaches its peak, or in the opposite extreme, the era when humanity was ruled by the star-crossing gods. And replicating key elements such as treasures of equal value from Gilgamesh’s treasury as ingredients. Enkidu's most favored weapon to create is chains. They possess the ability to absorb energy and grow in strength and length in response. By creating these chains and enveloping them defensively, Enkidu is able to create barriers as large as a building, able to absorb high density Energy attacks. Enkidu is even able to combine this with their shapeshifting to form other attacks, such as merging with a bundle of countless chains to fire themself as a a high-density energy shell. Furthermore as Enkidu is an abnormality, it's in their nature to be effective even against the Fixers and Distortions. Carmen allow humans to have the power to distort now became the piercing power to reject Distortions. Enkidu is able to create certain weapons that siphon away distorted aura while undermining the Distortion. One such weapon being a massive harpoon with a massive chain that is fired from a cannon, the moment it lands near a Distortion's temple it is able to slowly tear away at their psychological collapse and siphon the Distortion from them.

Body Transfiguration: Enkidu does not possess normal parameters, instead of possessing Body Transfiguration as an inherent characteristic of an "Automatic Doll." A unique ability that allows Enkidu to allotted their Parameters; Strength, Endurance, Speed, Energy and Durability, from a set pool of points according to the situation. The higher the rank, the greater the pool. Since Enkidu is classified as ALEPH, all their parameters are ranked ALEPH by default. The cost, however, rises when bringing a parameter from ALEPH-rank to ALEPH +, which requires a two rank drop in another parameter, or a one rank drop in two parameters, to achieve. Enkidu possesses a comprehensive value of 30, and each parameter consumes the respective values: A-7, B-6, C-5, D-4, E-3. The maximum value is dependent on what Enkidu has. But against Gilgamesh’s Apsû, then all of Enkidu's parameters would be set to A rank and they would be given an additional 30 points to spend freely. With these extra points, Enkidu would be able to reach A+ in all parameters to counterbalance Gilgamesh Aluma Alish with his own.

Presence Detection: Enkidu boasts the highest rank of presence detection, a subsystem that allows him to become one with the World and identify anything out of place at long range, the closest demonstration of this long range is just pass half of the City. Via the Earth, is able to sense the presence of things at long range. It is why it effectively impossible to surprise attack Enkidu or go unnoticed by him even if they happen to be 5 kilometres away so long they still touched the ground they stand on and nearly everything connected it and with the only flaw that he can’t detect thing high in the air. This is shown when Shi Association when they had numerous of same Long Green-Haired Figure bumping into them. Even times District B surveillances show Enkidu turning his head to the camera “the same time” they tried to survey him as if he detected it. Even if for an instant, they may be able to evade an enemy's attacks the dust of debris in the air which how he was able time his Aeon of Babylon’s weapons against Gilgamesh’s Coronation of Babylon barrage.

Perfect Form: By making use of the energy of the land, they restore themself to their former shape. So long there is a supply of energy from the land, Enkidu’s body will never collapse. A powerful regeneration・restoration ability that is completely unprecedented. However, the Soul is a different matter.

E.G.O MANIFESTATION
Aluma Alish: is the E.G.O Manifestation of Enkidu, where they transform their own body into a Construct, to fire a giant amount of energy that pierces and binds the opponent in one hit. Originally, Enkidu was an abnormality capable of “restraining Gilgamesh.” However, Enkidu became Gilgamesh’s friend and, just like their friend wished, chose the path of using this “chain that restrains even Distortions” for the sake of the people. Upon manifesting it, Enkidu awakens the “breath of the planet” and transforms their own clay body into a Construct. energy surges from the earth and gathers around them in a colossal lance of light, wreathed in golden chains that pierce and bind their target. The E.G.O can draw on the planet, gaining power in response to threats who stronger than his baseline.  Enkidu drives this lance straight into the overloaded rupturing attack unleashed by Gilgamesh’s Apsû. As it advances, it stitches together the ruptures Apsû has torn in the World, until the two attacks meet head-on and cancel each other out. It could also be said that his E.G.O — an attack that used his own body as a weapon - was best personified. They would simply puncture the World and stitch it back together and is perfect counterbalance to Gilgamesh’s Apsû.
